{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:693c559e842aadf93ddcaba5f140c97aac1419c23fda3c1038c7a690c13b1213", "sample_idx": 27, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Section 1\nThe Guardian newspaper has issued corrections to several articles published on August 25th. These corrections address inaccuracies in reporting, ranging from details about individuals to factual errors within stories. The corrections aim to ensure the accuracy and integrity of the information presented to readers. The newspaper encourages readers to note these changes and appreciate their commitment to journalistic precision. This demonstrates a dedication to responsible reporting and a willingness to rectify mistakes promptly. \n\n***\n\nSection 2\nOne correction clarified the scope of a new pet theft law, stating it applies specifically to England and Northern Ireland, not the entire UK. Another corrected a description of Eileen Burbidge, the executive director of Fertifa, clarifying that Tony Chen and Nick Kuan are the company’s founders, not Burbidge. The newspaper also corrected a reference to Juliet Stevenson’s recent work, noting it was with director Alex Lawther, not \"Lowther\". A factual error was also corrected in the article about the family in the film Bend It Like Beckham, stating they are Sikh, not Muslim.\n\nSection 3\nFurther corrections were made regarding reporting on Venetia Stanley’s family history, clarifying that her uncle, the third Baron Stanley, converted to Islam, not her father, the fourth Baron. The article also corrected the phrase \"Asquith's wild trysts with his socialite mistress\". The corrections span various articles covering topics such as crime, business, film, and historical figures, underscoring the breadth of the newspaper’s coverage. The paper provides multiple ways for readers to contact the Readers' Editor to provide feedback or report further errors.\n\nSection 4\n* The newspaper is committed to accuracy and transparency in its reporting.\n* Readers are encouraged to refer to the corrections for the most accurate information.\n\nWrite to the Readers’ Editor, the Observer, York Way, London N1 9GU, email observer.readers@observer.co.uk, tel 020 3353 4736\n\n\n\nP.P.S. The listed articles and corrections are examples of the newspaper's ongoing efforts to maintain journalistic standards and provide reliable information to its readership.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Section", "logprob": -0.00033802041434682906}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.3870837688446045}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -0.0902138277888298}, {"token": "▁Guardian", "logprob": -0.010278741829097271}, {"token": "▁newspaper", "logprob": -0.46665817499160767}, {"token": "▁has", "logprob": -0.03228910267353058}, {"token": "▁issued", "logprob": -0.03366444259881973}, {"token": "▁corrections", "logprob": -0.586992084980011}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.010051821358501911}, {"token": "▁several", "logprob": -0.0001839230244513601}, {"token": "▁articles", "logprob": -0.04625182971358299}, {"token": "▁published", "logprob": -2.2053474822314456e-05}, {"token": "▁on", "logprob": -0.0006017066189087927}, {"token": "▁August", "logprob": -6.913899414939806e-05}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "2", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "5", "logprob": -3.6954811548639555e-06}, {"token": "th", "logprob": -1.9073468138230965e-06}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.011023455299437046}, {"token": "▁These", "logprob": -0.011533842422068119}, {"token": "▁corrections", "logprob": -0.14349934458732605}, {"token": "▁address", "logprob": -0.22832420468330383}, {"token": "▁inaccuracies", "logprob": -0.2580287456512451}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": -0.8340970873832703}, {"token": "▁reporting", "logprob": -0.025648945942521095}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.7905122637748718}, {"token": "▁ranging", "logprob": -1.5784578323364258}, {"token": "▁from", "logprob": -5.960462772236497e-0